@baseUrl = {{$dotenv BASE_URL}}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Auth
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cookies (access_token, refresh_token) are set by the server and stored
# automatically by REST Client's cookie jar. No manual token handling needed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────


### Register — creates a user and sets auth cookies
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "taiwokelvin@gmail.com",
  "name": "Taiwo Joseph",
  "password": "pass123@@"
}


### Login — validates credentials and sets auth cookies
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "taiwokelvin@gmail.com",
  "password": "pass123@@"
}


### Refresh Tokens — rotates the refresh token, issues a new access token
# Requires the refresh_token cookie (set after login or register).
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh


### Logout — invalidates the refresh token and clears cookies
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
